# CODEOWNERS — EXAMPLE, INERT BY ITS NAME.
#
# THIS FILE IS CALLED `CODEOWNERS.example` AND THAT IS THE WHOLE SAFETY MECHANISM.
# GitHub activates a file named exactly `CODEOWNERS` (in `.github/`, the repo root
# or `docs/`) THE MOMENT IT LANDS ON THE DEFAULT BRANCH — no setting, no
# confirmation. A kit that shipped the live name would silently make review
# assignments on every adopting repository, on behalf of teams that do not exist.
# Rename it yourself, deliberately, or not at all.
#
# EVERY HANDLE BELOW IS A PLACEHOLDER. There is no real user or team here: an
# unresolvable owner is INERT (GitHub simply assigns nobody), a real one you did
# not mean to name is a person getting review requests.
#
# WHAT IT IS WORTH WITHOUT THE RULESET: nothing enforceable. CODEOWNERS alone
# REQUESTS reviews; it BLOCKS a merge only when a ruleset (or branch protection)
# carries `require_code_owner_review`. The model in this directory ships that flag
# FALSE on purpose — turning it on without owners who can actually review is how a
# repository locks itself out. Decide the two together.
#
# Syntax note that costs an hour when missed: the LAST matching pattern wins, not
# the most specific one. Order from general to specific.

# Everything, unless a later line overrides it.
*                               @ORG/TEAM

# The pipeline's own contract surfaces. A change here changes how every agent on
# every host behaves, so it is the one place a second pair of eyes pays for itself.
/AGENTS.md                      @ORG/TEAM
/CLAUDE.md                      @ORG/TEAM
/.claude/agents/                @ORG/TEAM
/.codex/agents/                 @ORG/TEAM
/.gemini/agents/                @ORG/TEAM
/.github/agents/                @ORG/TEAM
/.kimi-code/agents/             @ORG/TEAM

# The deterministic guards. These REFUSE things; loosening one is not a detail.
/.claude/hooks/                 @ORG/TEAM
/.codex/hooks/                  @ORG/TEAM
/.githooks/                     @ORG/TEAM
/.agents/security/              @ORG/TEAM

# CI and the rules about the rules.
/.github/workflows/             @ORG/TEAM
/.github/rulesets/              @ORG/TEAM
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @ORG/TEAM
